# The production build's heap, and its ceiling. Node sizes the heap from the machine's
# memory (about a quarter of it), too small for this build even on CT210 (2 GB). The
# ceiling matters as much: update.sh builds inside CT209 (1 GB) while Postgres and the live
# backend run there, and a build that outgrows its heap stops with Node's own heap error,
# which update.sh answers by going back to the previous commit, instead of growing until
# the kernel's OOM killer picks a process, Postgres or the backend among them.
# The build needs between 448 and 512 MB (measured in CT210, 2026-10-04) since the icon set
# is imported by name (src/components/shared/gameIcons.js) and Rollup's cache and the gzip
# size report are off (vite.config.js); this leaves it some room.
# npm passes this to the scripts it runs (npm run build), not to npm itself.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=576
